<title>PERU: Peru September molybdenum output falls 24.7 pct.</title>
<headline>Peru September molybdenum output falls 24.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's molybdenum output fell 24.7 percent to 226 tonnes in September, compared with the same month last year, according to preliminary figures from the Energy and Mines Ministry released Tuesday.</p>
<p>Production fell 2.7 percent to 2,345 tonnes in the first nine months of the year compared with the same period last year, the ministry said.</p>
<p>Molybdenum output rose 19.5 percent to 3,411 tonnes in 1995 compared with 2,854 tonnes during the previous year.</p>
<p>U.S.-based Southern Peru Ltd is Peru's main producer of molybdenum.</p>
<p>-- Saul Hudson, Lima newsroom 511 221-2134</p>
</text>
